  "scientific_summary": "347063 LITERAL LEAN ENDPOINTS PROVED, uncredited pending independent audit, paper and root adjudication. Root verified from receipts: Zeck.split_smallest_asymptotic, Zeck.combine_smallest_asymptotic with c = 5/2 - phi + the tsum over j of 1/F(2(j+2)), and Zeck.combine_constant_bracket 1.206 < c < 1.207, with the exact statements read in ZeckEndpoint.lean; axioms exactly propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound; six sealed baseline modules and fourteen new ones, each with compile, kernel and hash evidence. Nine failed compile attempts retained with true exits. The endpoint proof uses an integer counter with weights d_i = F_(i-2) - [i even] rather than the cycle balance, which is proved separately. The theorems bind to the source game from n copies of F_1, by the root's exact-source-scope ruling; the MathDB record's start position gives zero moves and that is proved. Unpaid: a single fresh extracted replay of the whole chain, independent formal audit, paper and root adjudication. Credit 0, 58/80.",
